cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  PhomiNeuro: a neural-field surrogate for time-resolved
  near-infrared fluence in the human head
message: >-
  If you use this software, the trained weights or the derived
  head models, please cite both this record and the paper it
  accompanies. Please also cite the upstream sources listed in
  the `references` section, whose terms require it.
type: software
authors:
  # TODO before deposit: complete the author list, ORCIDs and affiliations,
  # and make them identical to the manuscript's author list and order.
  - given-names: Sihan
    family-names: Dong
    email: sihan.dong@unibe.ch
    affiliation: University of Bern
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/dddshzy/myV18h3temp'
abstract: >-
  A neural-field surrogate that predicts time-resolved
  near-infrared fluence in anatomically realistic human head
  models at 810 nm. Conditioned on a frozen 3D medical-imaging
  foundation-model feature pyramid and on source-to-point path
  integrals referenced to the beam entry point, it is continuous
  in space and in time, so it can be queried at a single
  coordinate or at a time between the ten training gates --
  neither of which a fixed voxel-grid network can do. This
  record contains the inference package, three trained seeds
  (K=3000), the fine-tuned encoder adapter and demo head models.
keywords:
  - diffuse optics
  - near-infrared spectroscopy
  - Monte Carlo light transport
  - implicit neural representation
  - neural field
  - surrogate model
  - foundation model
  - transcranial photobiomodulation
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: 'https://github.com/dddshzy/myV18h3temp/blob/main/LICENSE'
# The repository is NOT uniformly Apache-2.0. The field above describes the CODE,
# which is what CFF's single `license` key can express. Weights and derived data
# carry different terms -- notably the encoder adapter, which is a derivative of
# NVIDIA NV-Segment-CTMR and is therefore non-commercial. See NOTICE and DATA_CARD.md.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-08-14'
# doi: '10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX'   # fill in after the Zenodo deposit

